<% layout('/layouts/boilerplate') %>
<% title = "About Wanderlust" %>

<section class="about-hero">
    <span class="hero-label">ABOUT THE PROJECT</span>
    <h1>Travel planning made simple.</h1>
    <p>Wanderlust is a community-based accommodation platform where people can discover, share, and review unique places to stay.</p>
</section>

<div class="row g-4 about-content">
    <div class="col-lg-7">
        <h2>What can you do here?</h2>
        <p>Visitors can browse available listings, search by location and price, and open each listing to see its full description, host, and reviews.</p>
        <p>Registered users can add new listings, edit or remove their own listings, and share their experience through ratings and comments.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-5">
        <div class="about-panel">
            <h3>Project features</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Account signup and login</li>
                <li>Listing search and price sorting</li>
                <li>Create, edit, and delete listings</li>
                <li>Ratings and traveler reviews</li>
                <li>Responsive design for mobile screens</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="project-note">
    <h2>Built as a full-stack web project</h2>
    <p>Wanderlust uses Node.js, Express, MongoDB, Mongoose, EJS, Bootstrap, and Passport authentication to connect the user interface with a working backend.</p>
    <a href="/listings" class="btn btn-dark">Start exploring</a>
</section>
